            <div xml:id="d618">

                <pb facs="0616" n="604" xml:id="pg604"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.3300 Motomar/43: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico
                                City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-22T17:00:00-06:00">December 22, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>325. Your 248, December 21, 7 p.m. Boal spoke to Beteta yesterday morning and
                    today regarding this question and was assured that the Spanish Embassy planes
                    which have been stored in the sanitary warehouse at Vera Cruz were not being
                    sent out of Mexico.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
